<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia's Jan 1-15 palm oil exports 255,320t - SGS.</title>
<headline>Malaysia's Jan 1-15 palm oil exports 255,320t - SGS.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo surveyor Societe Generale de Surveillance (SGS) Malaysia Sdn Bhd said on Thursday it estimated Malaysia's palm oil exports for January 1-15 at 255,320 tonnes against 406,924 in December 1-15.</p>
<p>It said the exports comprised 44,672 tonnes of RBD palm oil, 109,816 tonnes of RBD palm olein and 42,839 tonnes of RBD palm stearin. The other products amounted 57,993 tonnes.</p>
<p>India was the main buyer during the period, taking 52,500 tonnes, followed by China (20,125 tonnes), Indonesia (15,500 tonnes) and South Africa (12,850 tonnes).</p>
<p>Countries in the European Union bought 69,395 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-8911)</p>
